---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import dock from "../assets/dock.png";
import gifts from "../assets/gifts.png";
import events from "../assets/events.png";
import display from "../assets/display.png";
import counters from "../assets/counters.png";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Base title="LiveBridge for OBS Studio" description="One private timeline of chat, events and gifts for TikTok LIVE and YouTube Live, as docks inside OBS Studio.">

<header class="hero"><div class="wrap">
<span class="pill"><i></i> Early access · Windows installer for OBS Studio</span>
<h1>Your whole live, in <em>one timeline</em>.</h1>
<p class="lead">Chat, gifts, follows, Super Chats and live counters from TikTok LIVE and YouTube Live, side by side, as docks inside OBS Studio. Private by design: nothing leaves your computer.</p>
<div class="cta"><a class="btn primary" href="#features">See what it does</a><a class="btn ghost" href={base+"privacy/"}>How your data is handled</a></div>
<div class="platforms"><img src={base+"brand/tiktok.svg"} alt=""><img src={base+"brand/youtube.svg"} alt=""><span>TikTok LIVE and YouTube Live today · Twitch and Kick later</span></div>
<div class="shots">
<div class="frame"><Image src={gifts} alt="Gifts dock with real TikTok gift pictures" widths={[480,720,900]} sizes="(max-width: 860px) 100vw, 480px" /></div>
<div class="frame big"><Image src={dock} alt="The LiveBridge dock in OBS Studio" widths={[480,720,900]} sizes="(max-width: 860px) 100vw, 480px" /></div>
<div class="frame"><Image src={events} alt="Events dock" widths={[480,720,900]} sizes="(max-width: 860px) 100vw, 480px" /></div>
</div>
<p class="cap">Screenshots use demo data (a test run of the app). Gift and sticker pictures are the real ones from TikTok.</p>
</div></header>

<section id="features"><div class="wrap">
<span class="kicker">What it does</span>
<h2>Everything a streamer needs to see, in one place.</h2>
<p class="sub">Stop jumping between the TikTok app, YouTube Studio and three browser tabs.</p>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card"><div class="ico">💬</div><h3>One private timeline</h3><p>Chat from every connected platform in a single list, with badges, emotes and stickers as viewers see them.</p></div>
<div class="card"><div class="ico">🎁</div><h3>Real gifts</h3><p>Gifts show their own picture, name and count. Small gifts and big ones (500+ diamonds) have their own look. Super Chats and new members too.</p></div>
<div class="card"><div class="ico">📊</div><h3>Live counters</h3><p>Viewers, likes, new followers, diamonds, Super Chats and members, grouped by platform and updated as they change.</p></div>
<div class="card"><div class="ico">👋</div><h3>Follows, shares, bans</h3><p>New followers and subscribers, shares, and YouTube bans and timeouts, as quiet little events in the chat.</p></div>
<div class="card"><div class="ico">⚡</div><h3>Activity line</h3><p>Under the chat, one line shows who just joined, followed, shared or liked, rotating calmly one at a time.</p></div>
<div class="card"><div class="ico">🧩</div><h3>Docks that fit your layout</h3><p>Use the main dock alone, or add separate Gifts and Events docks and place them anywhere in OBS.</p></div>
</div></div></section>

<section class="alt" id="custom"><div class="wrap">
<span class="kicker">Customize</span>
<h2>Show what you want. Hide what you don't.</h2>
<p class="sub">Every part of the chat can be turned on or off from a clear Settings screen. Nothing is taken away unless you say so.</p>
<div class="split">
<div><div class="frame"><Image src={display} alt="Display settings" widths={[480,720,900]} sizes="(max-width: 860px) 100vw, 480px" /></div></div>
<div><h3 style="font-size:24px">Display, in three simple blocks</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Main Chat.</b> Choose between chat messages, gifts and support, and follows, shares and bans.</li>
<li><b>Above the Main Chat.</b> An optional events area like TikTok's own: show all events, only follows and shares, or only gifts and members. Drag the bar to make it bigger.</li>
<li><b>Under the Chat.</b> The activity line, on or off.</li>
<li><b>Test the whole chat.</b> One button runs a short demo for the platforms you connected, so you can check your layout before going live.</li>
</ul></div></div>
<div class="split rev" style="margin-top:56px">
<div><h3 style="font-size:24px">Counters, platform by platform</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Hide a whole platform</b> or pick the exact numbers you want.</li>
<li><b>Each number belongs to a platform</b>, so you never wonder where it comes from.</li>
<li><b>Only connected platforms</b> appear at the top and bottom of the dock.</li>
</ul></div>
<div><div class="frame"><Image src={counters} alt="Counter settings" widths={[480,720,900]} sizes="(max-width: 860px) 100vw, 480px" /></div></div></div>
</div></section>

<section><div class="wrap">
<span class="kicker">Connecting</span>
<h2>No passwords. No servers. Two minutes.</h2>
<div class="two" style="margin-top:28px">
<div class="card"><h3><img src={base+"brand/tiktok.svg"} alt="" width="18" height="18" style="vertical-align:-3px;border-radius:4px"> TikTok</h3><p>Type your username and press Connect. LiveBridge reads the same public data a viewer of your live sees. No TikTok password is ever asked.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3><img src={base+"brand/youtube.svg"} alt="" width="18" height="18" style="vertical-align:-3px;border-radius:4px"> YouTube</h3><p>Sign in with Google in your browser. Only one permission is requested: read-only access to your YouTube account, to read your own live chat and counters. You can disconnect, and revoke it at Google, from Settings.</p></div>
</div></div></section>

<section class="alt"><div class="wrap">
<span class="kicker">Privacy</span>
<h2>Runs on your computer. Period.</h2>
<p class="sub">There is no LiveBridge server, no account and no analytics.</p>
<div class="priv">
<div class="card"><div class="big">127.0.0.1</div><p>The helper service listens only on your own computer. Nobody on your network can reach it.</p></div>
<div class="card"><div class="big">0</div><p>Accounts, servers, trackers or ads. We never receive your chat, your tokens or your data.</p></div>
<div class="card"><div class="big">Read-only</div><p>On YouTube the app can only read. It never posts, deletes or changes anything.</p></div>
</div>
<p style="margin-top:22px"><a href={base+"privacy/"}>Read the full Privacy Policy →</a></p>
</div></section>

<section><div class="narrow faq">
<span class="kicker">Questions</span>
<h2>FAQ</h2>
<details><summary>Which platforms are supported?</summary><p>TikTok LIVE and YouTube Live. Twitch and Kick are planned but not available yet.</p></details>
<details><summary>Which systems?</summary><p>The installer is for Windows and OBS Studio. It finds your OBS folder and lets you confirm or change it before installing anything.</p></details>
<details><summary>Windows says the app is unknown. Is it safe?</summary><p>The installer is not code-signed yet, so Windows SmartScreen may warn you. Choose "More info" then "Run anyway". The plugin only runs inside OBS and talks only to TikTok and Google.</p></details>
<details><summary>Does it send my chat anywhere?</summary><p>No. Everything stays on your computer. See the <a href={base+"privacy/"}>Privacy Policy</a>.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can it moderate my chat?</summary><p>Not yet. It shows what happens (for example YouTube bans and timeouts) but it does not act on your behalf.</p></details>
<details><summary>Why does TikTok show fewer details than the TikTok app?</summary><p>TikTok does not offer an official live API. LiveBridge reads the public data of your live, so some app-only items (for example some emoji codes) can look different.</p></details>
</div></section>
</Base>
